problem:
Problem description
- There are $$T$$ planning stages indexed by $$t \in \{1,\ldots,T\}$$.
- At each stage $$t$$, the factory requires $$R_t$$ usable special tools.
- The tool requirement profile over the horizon is given by the demand sequence $$\{R_t\}_{t=1}^T$$.
- After a tool is used in a stage, it must leave service and be routed to one of two repair modes before it can be used again.
- The two repair modes are:
  - a slow repair mode with unit repair cost $$b$$ and return delay $$p$$ stages,
  - a fast repair mode with unit repair cost $$c$$ and return delay $$q$$ stages,
  - where the slow repair mode is cheaper but slower, and the fast repair mode is faster but more expensive.
- New tools may be purchased at unit cost $$a$$, and new purchases are the most expensive source of tools.
- The planning horizon ends after stage $$T$$, so any tool returning after stage $$T$$ has no value for feasibility inside the horizon.
- Optional capacity limits, if provided, are represented by stage-dependent limits such as $$K_t^{\mathrm{buy}}$$, $$K_t^{\mathrm{slow}}$$, and $$K_t^{\mathrm{fast}}$$; otherwise, no explicit capacity limit is imposed.
- The objective is to minimize the total tool-related spending over the horizon, including new purchases and repair actions.
- The business rules are:
  - every stage demand must be fully satisfied,
  - every tool used in a stage must be assigned to exactly one repair mode afterward,
  - repaired tools become available again only after their corresponding delay,
  - tools available at a stage come from earlier purchases and from repairs that have already returned,
  - all decision quantities are nonnegative integers.
- A solution is represented by:
  - the purchase plan $$\{x_t\}_{t=1}^T$$, where $$x_t$$ is the number of new tools bought at stage $$t$$,
  - the slow-repair assignment plan $$\{y_t^{\mathrm{slow}}\}_{t=1}^T$$, where $$y_t^{\mathrm{slow}}$$ is the number of tools sent to slow repair after stage $$t$$,
  - the fast-repair assignment plan $$\{y_t^{\mathrm{fast}}\}_{t=1}^T$$, where $$y_t^{\mathrm{fast}}$$ is the number of tools sent to fast repair after stage $$t$$,
  - the implied availability profile $$\{I_t\}_{t=1}^T$$, where $$I_t$$ is the number of tools available at the start of stage $$t$$,
  - the total cost $$Z$$ over the planning horizon.

Input Format
{
  "planning_horizon": "$$T$$",
  "demand": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "[$$T$$]",
    "meaning": "$$R_t$$ is the number of tools required at stage $$t$$"
  },
  "purchase_cost": "$$a$$",
  "slow_repair": {
    "unit_cost": "$$b$$",
    "return_delay": "$$p$$"
  },
  "fast_repair": {
    "unit_cost": "$$c$$",
    "return_delay": "$$q$$"
  },
  "initial_available_tools": {
    "symbol": "$$I_1$$",
    "type": "integer",
    "default": "$$0$$",
    "meaning": "the number of usable tools available at the start of stage $$1$$"
  },
  "optional_capacities": {
    "purchase_capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$K_t^{\\mathrm{buy}}$$",
      "type": "array or scalar",
      "default": "unbounded",
      "meaning": "maximum number of tools that can be purchased at stage $$t$$"
    },
    "slow_repair_capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$K_t^{\\mathrm{slow}}$$",
      "type": "array or scalar",
      "default": "unbounded",
      "meaning": "maximum number of tools that can be sent to slow repair at stage $$t$$"
    },
    "fast_repair_capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$K_t^{\\mathrm{fast}}$$",
      "type": "array or scalar",
      "default": "unbounded",
      "meaning": "maximum number of tools that can be sent to fast repair at stage $$t$$"
    }
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "total_cost": "$$Z$$",
  "purchase_plan": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "[$$T$$]",
    "meaning": "$$x_t$$ is the number of new tools purchased at stage $$t$$"
  },
  "slow_repair_plan": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "[$$T$$]",
    "meaning": "$$y_t^{\\mathrm{slow}}$$ is the number of tools sent to slow repair after stage $$t$$"
  },
  "fast_repair_plan": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "[$$T$$]",
    "meaning": "$$y_t^{\\mathrm{fast}}$$ is the number of tools sent to fast repair after stage $$t$$"
  },
  "availability_profile": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "[$$T$$]",
    "meaning": "$$I_t$$ is the number of tools available at the start of stage $$t$$"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "planning_horizon": 10,
  "demand": [3, 5, 2, 4, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1],
  "purchase_cost": 10,
  "slow_repair": {
    "unit_cost": 1,
    "return_delay": 3
  },
  "fast_repair": {
    "unit_cost": 3,
    "return_delay": 1
  },
  "initial_available_tools": 0
}
